{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And they placed him in custody.</b> Rashi explained: they did not place the wood-gatherer with him [the blasphemer], for both were in one chapter, etc. And if you ask: but Rashi already explained above, 'he went out — from where did he go out? Rabbi Levi says: from his world he went out. Rabbi Berakhiah says: from the section above he went out, to heckle him' — and he said, 'on the day of the sabbath, on the day of the sabbath you shall arrange it' etc. — and we know that the showbread was not made until the second year, when the Tabernacle was erected, and the wood-gatherer desecrated the sabbath of the second year of the first year, as we say, and if so, how were they in one chapter? One may answer that the section of the showbread written here, in the chapter of the wood-gatherer, was stated [together with it], and there is no earlier and later in the Torah, and it was [written] above in order to heckle him — 'son of an Egyptian man.'" "<b>To explain to them according to the word of YHWH.</b> It appeared to them that he was liable to stoning, as it is written ״אביו ואמו קלל דמיו בו״ — a fortiori for the Shekhinah. But punishments are not derived from a fortiori reasoning, and therefore it is written: to explain to them according to the word of YHWH."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The phrase 'השניה של שנה ראשונה' is awkward; translated hyper-literally. The phrase 'ועליה לגלג אותו' — the antecedent of עליה (the feminine section/verse written above) and the object אותו (him, the blasphemer) are both retained as found."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:58.356573954Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}